{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/416820-if-the-slender-man-was-a-true-fae-what-would-his-realm-be-like","id":416820,"title":"If the Slender Man was a True Fae, what would his Realm be like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-23T13:24:38-08:00","id":416820,"title":"If the Slender Man was a True Fae, what would his Realm be like?","content":"In my game, we will go to the Slender Man's Arcadian Realm to rescue someone. I only have vague ideas, like a surrealist, dark forest with decaying buildings here and there. I'd appreciate suggestions for what hobgoblins and changelings might be encountered there. Lastly, I'd like to know what you think the Slender Man's fighting style would be like (I'm thinking about quick, stealthy attacks combined with illusions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:41:44-08:00","id":416854,"title":"","content":"Everything is taller than you thought it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:59:19-08:00","id":416866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/416820-if-the-slender-man-was-a-true-fae-what-would-his-realm-be-like?p=416854#post416854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything is taller than you thought it was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! That brings to mind several images that are both weird and kind of funny.<br /> <br /> I assume there would be Lurkgliders that fly from tree to building, Steepscramblers that live on the outer walls or branches, Moonborns who have been driven insane by trying to predict where Slendy would be next, Gargantuans/Woodbloods that look like bizarre pseudo trees and Playmates/Palewraiths that participate in Slendy's twisted notion of hide and seek. Maybe some Chirurgeons/Razorhands that are forced to dissect people and put their organs on plastic bags and place them on trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:34:01-08:00","id":416928,"title":"","content":"While I was never all that big a follower of the whole Slenderman thing, from what I get of it, the sheer lack of knowledge about anything about Slenderman seems to be the biggest thing about the creature. That is, what makes it creepy is that it's the monster you don't see, because Nothing Is Scarier...<br /> <br /> I remember reading in Autumn Nightmares about &quot;The Shadow&quot; type of Gentry. Shadows don't make palaces, they don't work the ones they take as slaves... They just keep them trapped in their lands, and <i>watch</i>. <br /> <br /> An Arcadian realm is basically a dream, the dream of a creature made of dreams, and where all the same rules of dreams apply. In fact, in my own headcanon, one of the primary reasons why any Gentry takes humans is because their dreams aren't real, and will dissipate without someone watching them at all times. It's the only way to enforce stability on their subjective reality. They take humans and force them to be trees in their forests, because without at least one REAL tree, then the forest would go away as soon as the Gentry stepped out. The human-turned-tree is there just to keep looking at the other trees, and make them still exist by constantly confirming their existence. But more importantly, as the dream of a dream, it is best to think of the realm of a Gentry as being more like their own bodily organ than as their home. To rearrange the landscape or even laws of physics within their realm is like flexing a muscle to them. In Its realm, you only see what It wants you to see. And Slenderman never wants to be seen by anyone for anything more than a half-seen glimpse before it all goes black... After all, the nightmare is the source of his power. It doesn't need a house, it just needs its food and its purpose, and its food is fear, and its purpose is to perfect the art of the Nightmare. <br /> <br /> Hence, I wouldn't think of the Slenderman's realm as one where you have a bunch of random changelings all just hanging out or even doing grizzly things. <br /> <br /> Slenderman's realm is one of utter lonesomeness and isolation. <br /> <br /> When you step in, all color dies. The world of The Slenderman is one of pure black and white, just as no color clings to him. It is dark. No light you bring with you seems to matter much, as if the light simply refuses to function in Its realm. It is a world of monochrome silhouette and shadow. Many vertical shadows. It is a dark forest, although beyond a few dozen feet, one can hardly see anything, but where there is the weak, pale light of an eternally overcast sky peeking through the pitch-black clutches of the canopy of the trees. If you wander, however, even that seems to change. You aren't sure at what point you entered a cave, but suddenly, looking at them again, what is around you are the stalagmites of a cave, not trees, and you could hardly even notice when they weren't the small splotches of light flickering through either leaves or the dead branches of trees, but the occasional holes in the cavern ceiling letting just a glimpse of sunlight through... that IS sunlight, yes? You'd hate to think you're down so deep, it's merely the reflection of some light fixture or glowing crystal thing. The stalagmites (and trees, for that matter) seem preternaturally slick, in any event, and are impossible to climb, and you never seemed to have found any walls or even a downward slope. You can't be sure of anything much beyond a dozen feet or so in front of you, as it all is just barely-glimpsed reflections of light giving a black-and-white outline of the edges of something, and it isn't until you really look at something up close that you can really tell what it is... and by then, there's usually something else clawing at your attention. Strange shapes keep moving, only to be a branch in the wind. A human shape you could have sworn was moving was an old, discarded jacket clinging to a spike of stalagmite.<br /> <br /> Your other senses seem muted, as well. The smell is that of... old. Dust, wet dirt, dead leaves, the scent of limestone dripping on a cavern floor.<br /> <br /> It's cold and wet. A wetness that seeps through anything you wear to bring the cold into your bones. <br /> <br /> Then, there are the sounds. The constant drip of water. The whistling of the wind. Some gravel crunching as it rolls down some of those slopes you swear must be around here somewhere, yet never actually find, yourself. Or was it crunching underfoot? They somehow echo from everywhere, even when there are no walls. They always sound muted, almost like it's being played back as a recording, and from far away. Even your own voice, if you shout out, seems to be coming from some faded vinyl record player somewhere far off. <br /> <br /> You KNOW there has to be someone living in here. You keep seeing the signs of life. But it's always the pale white bones you at first thought were just fallen tree limbs, only to trip on them and see they had been shattered open so as to suck out their marrow. In the poor light, you can't even tell what gouged those bones, if they were claws or blades, or if they were before or after the death. Perhaps it was just clawed by a scavenger come long after the kill? <br /> <br /> You tried to stay together. You never would have left each other's side, but the realm itself seemed to FORCE you apart at every step. A slick patch of ground sent the legs flying out from under one of your number, and they slid down away. What shouts they made seemed to come from no direction in particular, and soon were to distant to make out, even though you had hardly moved. Worse still, you couldn't even find where they were standing when they slipped, as it all seems solid, now... In the frantic search for the missing member of your group, another of yours went beyond the dark haze-out, and though you could swear you kept your eyes on the silhouette at all times, you reached out for what turned out to be a shrub rustling in the wind. The voice had by then trailed somehow further away into being just more of the echos.<br /> <br /> You can't tell about anything for certain in this maze without walls, but somehow, it seems to get more... hostile. You hear things that sound ever more like the grunts of a wild beast when you listen to the wind, but can't make out direction or distance. Strange shapes blur between the vertical shadows, but you can never make out what they were, and if you ever do pounce upon them, it's always just another picked-over corpse or the tattered clothes of someone that previously passed through here lying strung out. Why are there so many clothes around, anyway? Did someone try to leave a trail of breadcrumbs through this forest? Any further thought on it fades as you hear another growl, somehow closer, and from every direction, but definitely not in front of you, and there's nothing behind, as well...<br /> <br /> Somehow, you're in the forest again? Or is it a new forest? You can't tell.<br /> <br /> Then, when you are about to pass through two narrow trees, you suddenly realize that they aren't shaped like the rest, and they're bending... And then, through the dark haze above, there are five long stalagmites bearing down upon you, and you realize, &quot;Oh. Those aren't trees, they're legs.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:48:36-08:00","id":416936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <